//? Title: Perceptron: actual margin-driven updates
//? Subtitle: Canonical C++ producers, original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
The producer starts weights and bias at zero and visits rows in supplied order.
A nonpositive signed margin triggers the additive weight and bias update. Only
an actual complete zero-update pass certifies convergence. A finite epoch budget
returns last weights for nonseparable data. Since the bias is trained, the
classical radius/margin bound concerns augmented vectors(x,1), and is neither a
finite-precision nor a held-out generalisation guarantee. The original
two-dimensional separable fixture isolates updates; contradictory controls
expose the cap.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and scope

The producer starts weights and bias at zero and visits rows in supplied order.
A nonpositive signed margin triggers the additive weight and bias update. Only
an actual complete zero-update pass certifies convergence. A finite epoch budget
returns last weights for nonseparable data. Since the bias is trained, the
classical radius/margin bound concerns augmented vectors(x,1), and is neither a
finite-precision nor a held-out generalisation guarantee. The original
two-dimensional separable fixture isolates updates; contradictory controls
expose the cap.

$$ y_i(w\cdot x_i+b)\le0\ \Longrightarrow\ w\leftarrow w+\eta y_i x_i,\quad b\leftarrow b+\eta y_i. $$

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native diagram use the same producing run. Captured records own
their values; the report does not reconstruct the algorithm.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/perceptron_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::perceptron_trace({{1}, {-1}}, {1, -1}, 5);
    std::print("| epoch | row | actual pre-score | update | actual post-weights | post-bias |\n| ---: | " "---: | ---: | --- | --- | ---: |\n");
    for (auto &r : t.visits)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | `{}` | {} |\n", r.epoch, r.row,
                   r.score, r.updated, r.weights, r.bias);
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("n0", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual visited examples\n{}", t.visits.size()));
    d.node("n1", {8, 0},
           std::format("Actual updates\n{}", t.model.total_mistakes));
    d.node("n2", {16, 0},
           std::format("Actual certified zero-update pass\n{}",
                       t.model.converged));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/perceptron_tiny.svg");
}
```
